o outbound lanes on a designated roadway. Activated Evaculanes allows the use of the road’s shoulder as a transportation lane during an evacuation.</SPAN></P><P><SPAN>Update Frequency: ongoing</SPAN></P><P><SPAN>Source: TxDOT Districts, Traffic Safety Division (TRF) and Travel Division (TRV)</SPAN></P><P><SPAN>Security Level: Public</SPAN></P></DIV></DIV></DIV>"],"idCredit":["TxDOT - TRF - Traffic Safety TRF_GIS@txdot.gov"],"useLimit":[],"otherConsts":[]},"temporal_qualification":"Statewide reference, not verified July 2024 operational status. Metadata item name HurricaneEvac20241106, CreaDate 20260611, ModDate 20250527 and SyncDate 20250522 are metadata strings, not a certified Beryl snapshot date.","meaning":"Source route designations only; Potential EvacuLanes and Potential Contraflow remain potential, with no activation claim","file":{"path":"routes.geojson","bytes":2186578,"sha256":"d53f07218929cc0d4a6a827deb32276db6c17def9b458d834ed652dd49c10041"}}